Rules (pre-registered, applied in priority order):

- R0_PIN: file hash must equal the census's `sha256` for that path (the census stores per-hit sha256 of the file). If mismatch → PIN_DRIFT (void).
- R1_NEGATIVE_SCOPE: if the window text (lines window expanded by ±2) contains any of: `anti_scope`, `not_this_class`, `forbidden_strengthenings`, `forbidden_weakenings`, `must_not_conflate`, `must_not`, `exclusions`, `rejected_ambiguous_tokens`, `ban`, `forbidden as a class`, `no artifact may use` → NEGATIVE_SCOPE.
- R2_DEFINITION: if the window contains definitional markers: `iff:`, `is defined`, `definition`, `meaning_`, `_definition`, `concept:`, `witness_type`, `status: "trap`, `criterion`, `definition.` etc. and contains no comparative relation token of form `(is|are|carries|runs) (strictly )?(stronger|weaker) (than|statement)` → DEFINITION.
- R3_HISTORICAL: if window contains a ledger marker: `f0_reading`, `lead_reading`, `was stronger`, `status: resolved`, `status: cleared`, `resolution:`, `found_by:`, `contract_divergences`, `rev2`..? plus the record id `D1`/`D2`/`D3` → HISTORICAL_MENTION.
- R4_META_RETRACTED: markers `retracted`, `superseded`, `corrected`, `was off-vocabulary`, `earlier ... error`, `[R2-16 corrected`, `void` → META_RETRACTED (only if no operative relation assertion in window).
- R5_OPERATIVE: window contains an assertive comparative with a class/variant subject: regex `(?P<subj>(this class|the class|class [A-Z]|AF-[A-Z0-9-]+|variant [A-Z]+|C0|C2|H2_loc|set-based reading|union reading)[^.;\n]{0,120}?(is|are|carries|runs|establishes)?\s*(strictly\s+)?(stronger|weaker|larger|smaller))` OR phrases `(strictly )?(stronger|weaker) (than|statement)`. Then determine truth direction:
  - If subject refers to C0 vs C2/H2_loc/C1: truth: C0 stronger (E_C2⊂E_H2loc⊂E_C0). Larger extension class = weaker statement.
  - If subject is SET/union vs SINGLEQ/single-q: truth: SET strictly weaker.
  - Else UNRESOLVED_SUBJECT → MANUAL_REVIEW.
  Then INVERTED if asserted direction contradicts truth, CORRECT if matches.

