Let me rewrite `omega(n)`:
```python
def omega(n):
    def le(a,b):
        if a[0]=="x" and b[0] in ("x","q"): return a[1] <= b[1]
        if a[0]=="q" and b[0]=="q": return a[1]==b[1]
        return False
    qs=[("q",j) for j in range(n)]
    xs=[("x",i) for i in range(n)]
    setread = all(any(le(x,q) for q in qs) for x in xs)
    # certificate that no (q_j,t0) covers the tail gamma[t0:]: for every candidate with j<n-1, t0<n-1
    # there is an index i>=t0 with gamma[i] not <= q_j
    certs=0; failures=[]
    for j in range(n-1):
        for t0 in range(n-1):
            i=max(t0,j+1)
            if i<n and not le(xs[i], qs[j]):
                certs+=1
            else:
                failures.append((j,t0))
    return setread, certs, failures
```
Then `single_q_tail_covers = bool(failures)` → False. Verdict ok requires setread and not failures.

